// Practice quiz: Installing Java and the IDE
// Formative, low-stakes retention practice. Titles name the objective id each item practises.

$CATEGORY: java-foundations/java-basics/installing-java-and-the-ide

::o2 compiler location::Which part of the Java toolchain contains the compiler javac? {
=The JDK (Java Development Kit)#Correct. The JDK holds javac, java and other development tools.
~A JRE (Java Runtime Environment)#Not quite. A runtime could only run programs; it never included javac.
~Apache Maven#Not quite. Maven is a build tool that calls the compiler from the JDK; it does not contain one.
~The IDE#Not quite. An IDE uses a JDK that you install or select; the compiler belongs to the JDK.
}

::o2 PATH order::PATH lists /usr/lib/jvm/java-17/bin before /opt/jdk-25/bin, and both folders contain java. Which Java runs when you type java -version? {
=Java 17, because the shell runs the first match in PATH order#Correct. The shell searches PATH from left to right and stops at the first folder that holds the command.
~Java 25, because the newest version always wins#Not quite. The shell does not compare versions; it only follows PATH order.
~Neither, because two matches cause an error#Not quite. Several matches are normal; the first one is used.
~Whichever was installed last#Not quite. Installation order does not matter, only the order of folders in PATH.
}

::o1 Maven not found::After extracting Maven, mvn -v prints command not found. What fixes it? {
=Add the bin folder of the extracted Maven directory to PATH, then open a new terminal or export PATH#Correct. Maven's install guide says to add its bin directory to PATH and confirm with mvn -v.
~Set JAVA_HOME to the Maven folder#Not quite. JAVA_HOME points to a JDK; Maven still needs its own bin folder on PATH.
~Reinstall the JDK#Not quite. The JDK is not the problem; the shell cannot find the mvn command.
~Run mvn from inside the src folder#Not quite. The current folder is not searched for commands; PATH is.
}

::o1 Maven and JAVA_HOME::JAVA_HOME is set to /opt/jdk-25, but the first java on PATH is Java 17. Which Java does mvn -v report? {
=Java 25, because Maven uses JAVA_HOME when it is set#Correct. Maven uses the Java in JAVA_HOME if it is set, otherwise the java found on PATH.
~Java 17, because PATH always wins#Not quite. That is what the plain java command uses, but Maven checks JAVA_HOME first.
~Both versions, one for compiling and one for running#Not quite. Maven runs with one Java.
~An error, because the two settings disagree#Not quite. This is a valid setup; JAVA_HOME simply takes priority for Maven.
}

::o3 project SDK::IntelliJ IDEA opened a Maven project, but the code is red and the project has no JDK. Where do you choose JDK 25 for the project? {
=File, Project Structure, Project, then the SDK list#Correct. The project SDK is set in the Project page of Project Structure; you can also add a JDK from disk there.
~Change PATH in the terminal and the IDE follows it#Not quite. The IDE keeps its own JDK list, separate from your terminal's PATH.
~Edit the src folder name#Not quite. Folder names do not choose a JDK.
~Reopen only the Main.java file#Not quite. Opening one file does not import the Maven project or set its SDK.
}
